          "quote": "Input a finite regular oriented link diagram $D$ with $a$ arcs and $c$ crossings,\nfixed finite orderings of its arcs and crossings, and an odd prime $p$. The algorithm returns the full set\n$\\operatorname{Col}_p(D)$ of assignments of residues in $\\mathbb F_p$ to the\narcs satisfying the Fox crossing equations, together with\n$|\\operatorname{Col}_p(D)|$.\n\n1. Create one variable $x_j$ for each arc in the supplied order, and process\n   crossings in the supplied order.\n2. At each crossing with overarc $o$ and the two underarcs $i$ and $j$, append\n   the homogeneous linear equation $2x_o-x_i-x_j=0$ over $\\mathbb F_p$.\n   At a crossing, add the coefficients of any repeated arc in that row.\n3. Starting with the first column and first unused row, scan columns from left\n   to right. In a column with a nonzero entry in an unused row, choose the\n   first such row, swap it into the next pivot row, divide it by its nonzero\n   pivot, and add multiples of it to every other row to clear that column.\n   Advance the pivot row by one. If the column has no such entry, leave it\n   free and continue to the next column.\n4. After all columns have been processed, assign every free variable\n   independently any value in $\\mathbb F_p$ and solve the reduced equations\n   for the pivot variables. Return each resulting assignment once and the\n   number returned.",
