          "fact": "A2",
          "source": "alg-knot-wirtinger-presentation-from-code",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Define a finite procedure $\\mathsf{Wirtinger}(D,a_0)$ on a finite planar code $D$ for one oriented knot and a designated under-arc $a_0$ as follows. First check that the incidence data pair all half-edges, every crossing has exactly one over-branch and one under-branch, edge orientations join coherently, the code has one component, and its rational polygonal drawing certificate passes the finite segment-intersection checks. If any check fails, return `invalid-input`. Otherwise traverse the oriented knot once starting at $a_0$, label the maximal under-arcs $a_1,\\ldots,a_m$, and introduce one symbol $x_i$ for the positive meridian of each $a_i$. For each crossing $v$, read from its oriented local chart the over-arc $a_o$, the incoming and outgoing under-arcs $a_L,a_R$, and the conjugation direction supplied by the local meridian-conjugacy rule; append the single relator $x_o x_L x_o^{-1}x_R^{-1}$ or $x_o^{-1}x_Lx_ox_R^{-1}$ accordingly. Once a complement basepoint and basing paths to the meridians are fixed, interpret $x_i$ as the corresponding based positive meridian. Return the finite group presentation with generators $x_1,\\ldots,x_m$ and this one relator per crossing. The procedure uses only finite scans and terminates.",
